# inventory

Entrypoint: `src/main.js`, exporting `default async function (record, space)`.

It reads every `note` with `topic: 'inventory'`, pulls the first integer out of
each `message` (`'widget A: 3 in stock'` -> 3), sums them, and RETURNS a note
on topic `inventory-total` whose `message` is the total as a string.

Sandbox is `brokered-host` (see the `sandbox` record on the space). Available
calls, and nothing else:

- `space.query(pattern, limit) -> record[]` -- `pattern` is one object,
  `{kind, match}`; `match` is nested, not spread.
- `space.readOne(pattern) -> record | null`
- `space.put({kind, body}) -> {id}`

No fetch, no filesystem, no processes, no env, no console anybody reads. The
host stamps `team` and the parent links, so don't set them.

The returned value IS the result record. Returning it is what fences the
answer; putting it instead would not.

To change what counts as a stock number, edit `stockFromMessage`. To change
either topic, edit the constants at the top of `src/main.js`.
